Relevant columns and their typical purpose in this task  

• `posts_questions.id`: primary‑key of the question – needed to join to answers.  
• `posts_questions.accepted_answer_id`: the answer that was accepted – join to answers table.  
• `posts_questions.creation_date`: restrict questions to January 2016.  
• `posts_questions.tags`: check that the question is tagged with <javascript> and with at least one of <xss>, <cross-site>, <exploit>, <cybersecurity>.  
• `posts_questions.score`: required in final output.  
• `posts_questions.answer_count`: required in final output.  
• `posts_questions.view_count`: required in final output.  
• `posts_questions.comment_count`: required in final output.  
• `posts_questions.owner_user_id`: asker’s user id – join to `users` to read the asker’s reputation.  

• `posts_answers.id`: answer id (must match `accepted_answer_id`).  
• `posts_answers.creation_date`: restrict accepted answers to January 2016.  
• `posts_answers.owner_user_id`: answerer’s user id – join to `users`.  
• `posts_answers.score`: required in final output.  
• `posts_answers.comment_count`: required in final output.  

• `users.id`: primary‑key – join from question owner or answer owner.  
• `users.reputation`: asker’s / answerer’s reputation – required in final output.  

Important filter conditions that will be reused  

1. Question posted in January 2016    
   `posts_questions.creation_date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-02-01'`  

2. Accepted answer exists    
   `posts_questions.accepted_answer_id IS NOT NULL`  

3. Tags requirement    
   ```
   REGEXP_CONTAINS(posts_questions.tags , r'(?i)<javascript>') AND
   REGEXP_CONTAINS(posts_questions.tags , r'(?i)<(xss|cross-site|exploit|cybersecurity)>')
   ```  

4. Accepted answer also posted in January 2016  
   `posts_answers.creation_date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-02-01'`  


Below are ten exploratory SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows) that rise in complexity up to the complete query.  
Every identifier is wrapped in back‑ticks and all tables come from the only allowed dataset  
`bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow`.

```sql
-- 1. Look at January‑2016 questions tagged <javascript>
SELECT
  id,
  creation_date,
  tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE creation_date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-02-01'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags , r'(?i)<javascript>')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Same as #1 but also require at least one security‑related tag
SELECT
  id,
  tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE creation_date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-02-01'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags , r'(?i)<javascript>')
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags , r'(?i)<(xss|cross-site|exploit|cybersecurity)>')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Retrieve those questions plus their accepted answer id
SELECT
  id            AS question_id,
  accepted_answer_id,
  tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE accepted_answer_id IS NOT NULL
  AND creation_date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-02-01'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags , r'(?i)<javascript>')
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags , r'(?i)<(xss|cross-site|exploit|cybersecurity)>')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Join with the answers table to get the accepted answer row
SELECT
  q.id   AS question_id,
  a.id   AS answer_id,
  a.creation_date AS answer_created
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`  AS a
  ON a.id = q.accepted_answer_id
WHERE q.creation_date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-02-01'
  AND a.creation_date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-02-01'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(q.tags , r'(?i)<javascript>')
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(q.tags , r'(?i)<(xss|cross-site|exploit|cybersecurity)>')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Add answer and question scores
SELECT
  q.id   AS question_id,
  q.score AS question_score,
  a.id   AS answer_id,
  a.score AS answer_score
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`  AS a
  ON a.id = q.accepted_answer_id
WHERE q.creation_date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-02-01'
  AND a.creation_date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-02-01'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(q.tags , r'(?i)<javascript>')
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(q.tags , r'(?i)<(xss|cross-site|exploit|cybersecurity)>')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Bring in answerer reputation
SELECT
  a.id                    AS answer_id,
  u.reputation            AS answerer_reputation,
  a.score                 AS answer_score,
  a.comment_count         AS answer_comments
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`  AS a
  ON a.id = q.accepted_answer_id
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.users`          AS u
  ON u.id = a.owner_user_id
WHERE q.creation_date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-02-01'
  AND a.creation_date BETWEEN '2016-01-01' AND '2016-02-01'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(q.tags , r'(?i)<javascript>')
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(q.tags , r'(?i)<(xss|cross-site|exploit|cybersecurity)>')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Bring in asker reputation as well
